       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4000 mg per dose four times daily is 16,000 mg/day, which is five times the usual maximum for ibuprofen. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for outpatients, and 2,400 mg/day is the usual ceiling in most inpatient settings. A dose that high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular toxicity, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 4000 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly and give me a note for the order. I'd still recommend pharmacy review first."
